.TH PM_AUDIT 1 "March 2026" "v0.9.10" "PathMux Suite - Footage Auditor"
.SH NAME
pm_audit \- footage integrity checker for PathMux manifests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pm_audit
.RB [ \-\-deep ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ MID " | " MID : TID ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pm_audit
walks cached PathMux manifests and verifies that the source footage files
are still accessible and unmodified.  It catches common operational problems:
storage not mounted, SD card swapped or reformatted, files deleted or
corrupted.
.PP
Each trip contains a small validation sample — three footage files selected
at scan time with their MD5 checksums recorded in the manifest.
.B pm_audit
checks that each sample file still exists at the expected path and that its
checksum matches the recorded value.
.PP
.B pm_audit
does not write to any manifest.  It is purely read-only and safe to run at
any time, including from cron.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-deep
Also run
.BR ffprobe (1)
on every Front camera segment of every trip to detect truncated or corrupt
video files that pass the MD5 sample check.  This mode is significantly
slower on large collections — a confirmation prompt is shown before
proceeding when auditing more than five trips without a filter.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON output.  The top-level object contains
.BR total_trips ,
.BR problem_trips ,
.BR all_ok ,
and a
.B manifests
array.  Suitable for scripting and pipeline use.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the PathMux version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH "TRIP STATUS VALUES"
.TP
.B OK
All validation sample files are present and their MD5 checksums match
the values recorded at scan time.
.TP
.B MISSING
One or more validation files were not found on disk.  Typical causes:
storage drive not mounted, SD card removed, or files deleted.  The
filename of the first missing file is shown in parentheses.
.TP
.B MODIFIED
All validation files are present but at least one checksum does not match.
The file exists but its contents have changed since the manifest was written.
Typical causes: partial write during recording failure, filesystem
corruption, or deliberate replacement.
.TP
.B NO_VALIDATION
The trip has no validation sample recorded.  This affects trips scanned
before the validation feature was added.  Re-scan the footage path with
.B pathmux \-s
to populate validation data.
.TP
.B CORRUPT
.RB ( \-\-deep
only)  All validation sample checks passed but
.BR ffprobe (1)
reported an error or zero duration on a segment.  Indicates a truncated
or unreadable video file that happens not to be in the validation sample.
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Text (default)
.nf
[X1]  /z/srcdash/ex2
  X1  87  OK          2026-02-09  04:38:38  14 segs
  X1  37  MISSING     2026-02-10  14:31:41  16 segs  (Front/20260210_143141F.ts)

1 of 2 trips have problems.
.fi
.PP
A manifest header line
.RI ( [MID]\  path )
precedes each manifest's trips.
.SS JSON
.nf
{
  "all_ok": false,
  "total_trips": 2,
  "problem_trips": 1,
  "manifests": [
    {
      "id": "X1",
      "path": "/z/srcdash/ex2",
      "manifestFile": "/z/srcdash/ex2/pm_manifest_X1.json",
      "trips": [
        {
          "mid": "X1", "tid": "87",
          "date": "2026-02-09", "start_time": "04:38:38",
          "seg_count": 14,
          "status": "OK", "detail": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Audit all manifests:
.B pm_audit
.TP
Audit one manifest:
.B pm_audit X1
.TP
Audit one trip:
.B pm_audit X1:87
.TP
Deep check with ffprobe on all segments:
.B pm_audit --deep X1
.TP
Machine-readable output for scripting:
.B pm_audit --json
.TP
Use in a script — non-zero exit means problems:
.nf
pm_audit --json > audit.json
if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
    echo "Footage integrity problems found" >&2
fi
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pathmux/manifests.json
Manifest index.
.TP
.I <footage_path>/pm_manifest_<id>.json
Trip manifest containing the validation sample and checksums.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
All audited trips passed.
.TP
.B 1
One or more trips have a problem (MISSING, MODIFIED, NO_VALIDATION,
or CORRUPT).  Use
.B \-\-json
for machine-parseable detail.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pathmux (1),
.BR pm_ls (1),
.BR pm_gpsinfo (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by Stephen Berg, 2026.
